# Order of Operations: MOVE (domovement) fires before FOLLOW (moveblock).
# FOLLOW must track the target's POST-MOVE position, not its pre-move position.
#
# Rock IS MOVE facing right at (5,5). Baba IS FOLLOW ROCK at (6,5) — one tile ahead.
#
# Correct order (MOVE then FOLLOW):
#   MOVE: rock slides right from (5,5) → (6,5). Baba at (6,5) has no STOP/PUSH,
#         so rock lands on baba's tile (they coexist).
#   FOLLOW: rock is now at (6,5), same tile as baba → same-tile ignored → baba stays at (6,5).
#   Result: baba at (6,5), rock at (6,5).
#
# Wrong order (FOLLOW then MOVE — would be the bug):
#   FOLLOW: baba at (6,5) sees rock at (5,5) to the LEFT → baba moves LEFT to (5,5).
#   MOVE: rock at (5,5) slides right to (6,5) (baba at (5,5) is not STOP/PUSH).
#   Result: baba at (5,5), rock at (6,5) — assertion "at 6 5 baba" would FAIL.

[setup]
version 1
name "oop: move before follow (follow tracks post-move position)"

text 0 0 rock
text 1 0 is
text 2 0 move

text 0 1 baba
text 1 1 follow
text 2 1 rock

text 0 2 baba
text 1 2 is
text 2 2 you

object 5 5 rock right
object 6 5 baba right

[inputs]
wait

[expected]
at 6 5 baba
at 6 5 rock
not_won
